# SYNTHETIC example root manifest for offline contract generation tests.
# Every hash below is sha256('example:<path>'), NOT a real file. A contract
# generated from this file admits nothing real: it exists so the pipeline and
# the initramfs contract embedding can be exercised before rootfs-builder
# produces out/rootfs/rootfs.files.sha256. Never ship this contract to a device.
# Regenerate with: tools/build-root-contract.py --manifest <real manifest> ...
# contract v2 (ADR-0004 D2) topology paths below are synthetic too: the
# contract generator refuses to emit a contract for a manifest that lacks
# the declared PID1/login/Plasma/kernel-identity interface.  With these
# entries the synthetic manifest yields the same topology-only v2 contract
# (13 entries, 723 bytes, sha256 502f05f8...) as the real dev-v3 rootfs.
